; Find the next object that fits noun phrase 1 and passes the check
;
; Used by #R$7CCB to step through the candidates for the first noun phrase of a
; command. Each pass asks the lookup routine in IY (through #R$7CC9, with HL =
; RecBuf1, the phrase's words) for the next object, keeps it in FirstObject
; ($B6E8), sets bit 1 of RecWork ($793D: a candidate was found for phrase 1) and
; asks #R$94D6 whether that object lets the command through (it leaves the
; answer in ActionAllowed). A refused candidate is dropped and the next one is
; fetched, so the loop ends on the first accepted object or when the lookup is
; exhausted.
;
; IY Lookup routine: #R$9DD9 (objects around) or #R$9EA0 (exits), set by #R$7CCB
; IX Cursor of the lookup, kept by it between calls
; O:A $FF when no candidate is left, otherwise 1 (ActionAllowed)
; O:F Z when no candidate is left
; O:FirstObject The accepted object
@label=NextNoun1Match
c$7CFC LD HL,$7942   ;
 $7CFF CALL $7CC9             ; next candidate for phrase 1
 $7D02 CP $FF                 ; $FF: none left
 $7D04 RET Z         ;
 $7D05 LD ($B6E8),A           ; FirstObject
 $7D08 LD HL,$793D   ;
 $7D0B SET 1,(HL)             ; RecWork bit 1: phrase 1 has a candidate
 $7D0D CALL $94D6             ; does the verb allow it? (ActionAllowed)
 $7D10 LD A,($B6FB)  ;
 $7D13 AND A         ;
 $7D14 JR Z,$7CFC             ; refused: try the next one
 $7D16 RET           ;
